+|---|---|---|---|
+| Concurrency mechanism (see `decisions/concurrency-mechanism.md`) | Whole-visit revisions: each submission is an intact revision naming its base; concurrent submissions become competing revisions resolved by a coordinator | Field-aware three-way merge (combine disjoint field edits, review overlaps) | Field names do not reveal which observations are scientifically related, so an automatic merge could join a species identification from one worker with a cover estimate from another and produce a record no worker submitted, with no coordinator noticing. Whole-visit revisions keep each submitted visit intact and the path from a submitted observation to an exported value inspectable. They enlarge the coordinator review queue because even unrelated-field edits compete; that cost is accepted to avoid maintained merge rules. |
+| Submission shape | A complete visit per submission | Structured field changes / deltas | A whole visit preserves the worker's submission as a unit and needs no per-field merge logic. |
+| Idempotency | Idempotency key per submission | Deduplication by payload hash | Workers retry after offline connection failures; the key returns the original acceptance without creating a second stored edit. |
 
